WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.166 --> 00:00:02.602
-GOP members of Congress,

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:05.037
like Paul Gosar
and Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:00:05.037 --> 00:00:06.973
are facing growing scrutiny
over their roles

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:09.909
in the attempt to overthrow
our democracy on January 6th,

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:11.410
after a bombshell report
linked them

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.212
to the organizers
of the day's events.

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:15.314
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:19.786
[ Cheering and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:21.754
The stakes
of Joe Biden's presidency

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:23.622
and the Democrats' agenda
could not be higher.

00:00:23.622 --> 00:00:25.725
If Democrats don't deliver
on their promises

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:28.694
and fail to give voters a reason
to keep electing Democrats,

00:00:28.694 --> 00:00:31.597
then, the Republicans waiting
in the wings to take power

00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:32.798
are people like this --

00:00:32.798 --> 00:00:35.701
-Rudy Giuliani used a filter
to make himself

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:38.571
look like Abraham Lincoln
in an ad attack

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:41.540
on Virginia gubernatorial
candidate Terry McAuliffe.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:42.608
-Virginia,

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:45.911
[ Laughter ]
vote against the man

00:00:45.911 --> 00:00:51.117
who dishonored our past
by selling my bedroom

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.552
hundreds and hundreds of times

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:57.623
to scoundrels
in a pay-for-play scheme!

00:00:57.623 --> 00:00:59.592
In my time, we had a name

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:02.528
for men who sold bedrooms
for one night.

00:01:02.528 --> 00:01:04.831
In your time, the name is

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.466
Terry McAuliffe.

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:11.237
End the Clinton sleaze,
once and for all!

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:13.539
[ Laughter ]
-Wow. Disney's Haunted Mansion

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:14.774
really went all-out this year.

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:16.108
[ Laughter and applause ]
You know,

00:01:16.108 --> 00:01:17.776
you know you're a real scumbag

00:01:17.776 --> 00:01:20.746
when you can make
Abraham Lincoln seem dishonest.

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:22.681
[ Laughter and applause ]
That's Rudy Giuliani,

00:01:22.681 --> 00:01:24.350
former mayor
of America's largest city

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.518
and former personal attorney

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:26.852
to the president
of the United States.

00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:28.520
Although, he looks
more like a character

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:30.556
who got cut from "Oregon Trail"

00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:33.125
[ Laughter ]
because he gave
the kids nightmares.

00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:34.160
Whenever you encountered him,

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.564
a message would pop up
that says...

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:38.864
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.864 --> 00:01:40.834
Looks like the guy
you get your mission from in...

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:43.903
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:45.071
[ As Giuliani ]
Your next mission is

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:47.940
to whack Robert E. Lee.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.009
Then, go see Vito
down at the docks

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:51.811
and tell him it's done.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.213
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.213 --> 00:01:56.616
Also, what accent is he doing?

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:59.118
Is that supposed to be
19th-century American

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:01.354
or coma patient learning how
to talk again?

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:03.289
[ Laughter ]
If that's what Abe Lincoln

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:04.623
had actually sounded like,

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:07.060
the North would've given up
and lost the Civil War.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.761
[ As Giuliani ]
Four score and seven years ago,

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.463
somebody rented out my bedroom.

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:11.864
"This guy sucks!"

00:02:11.864 --> 00:02:12.931
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:12.931 --> 00:02:14.166
That's the modern GOP.

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:16.236
Sorry, that's the current GOP.

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:17.536
They tried to overthrow
an election,

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:19.739
based on bat[bleep]
conspiracy theories

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:21.474
from bamboo fibers on ballots

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:23.876
to Italian satellites
hacking voting machines,

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:27.279
to election software designed
by Hugo Chávez and the CIA

00:02:27.279 --> 00:02:29.282
to spread communism
around the world.

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:30.950
These are all things
they've actually said.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.518
I'm waiting for them
to claim, next,

00:02:32.518 --> 00:02:35.555
they saw thousands of people
vote twice using the Kanye mask

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:37.890
[ Laughter ]
and you wouldn't know
who it is

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.859
because they'd vote twice
for Kanye.

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:40.960
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.528
Arizona Congressman Paul Gosar,

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:44.664
one of the leaders of the
attempt to overturn the results,

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:46.265
said, in a recent
congressional hearing,

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:49.101
that mysterious, unnamed sources
had approached him

00:02:49.101 --> 00:02:50.403
the day after the election

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:52.704
to tell him the election
was stolen from Donald Trump.

00:02:52.704 --> 00:02:55.208
Now, don't worry about trying
to follow any of this,

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:56.876
because you can't.

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.611
-The day after the election,
I was contacted

00:02:58.611 --> 00:02:59.979
by two individuals.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.581
One had security and fraud,

00:03:02.581 --> 00:03:05.118
uh,

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:08.187
jobs with the banking world.

00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:09.788
The other one does fraud

00:03:09.788 --> 00:03:11.958
from the Department of Defense.

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:13.092
[ Laughter ]
What they saw from Arizona

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:15.461
and drew their attention
quickly, first.

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:17.463
They saw a numbers
of 90-some thousand

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:19.865
60-some thousand,
40-some thousand,

00:03:19.865 --> 00:03:23.435
ballots drop
into Donald Trump's category

00:03:23.435 --> 00:03:25.738
and then quickly
come out verbatim.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.239
[ Laughter ]
But then, they started watching

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:29.775
and looking to the dumps.

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:31.677
What I mean by that is,

00:03:31.677 --> 00:03:33.579
there's a first dump,
there's multiple dumps,

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:35.848
[ Laughter ]
maybe nine or 10
through the night.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.649
If the first dump
in Coconino County

00:03:37.649 --> 00:03:40.119
was 61% for Joe Biden,

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:42.021
you would expect,
the rest of the time,

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:45.524
the rest of the dumps,
to be very similar --

00:03:45.524 --> 00:03:49.462
[ Laughter ]
58%, 62%, 55%, and so on.

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:52.432
Not 40%, 38%, 35%.

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:53.499
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:56.168
That's drew a big
question mark to them.

00:03:56.168 --> 00:03:58.737
-Hey, man, if you're going
to talk about dumps that much,

00:03:58.737 --> 00:04:01.307
could you maybe move away
from the camera a little bit?

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:02.708
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.708 --> 00:04:03.976
Or just point it lower.

00:04:03.976 --> 00:04:06.813
Did you record this
on an ATM security camera?

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:08.247
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:09.982
Are you under the impression
that your forehead

00:04:09.982 --> 00:04:11.751
is your best feature?
It's not.

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:14.186
[ Laughter ]
And I say that as a person

00:04:14.186 --> 00:04:16.022
who has the same one.

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:17.823
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.823 --> 00:04:19.625
Also, I love the idea
that someone would find

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:22.929
rock-solid evidence that the
election was stolen and say,

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:24.396
"Hey, this is big.
Should we take it

00:04:24.396 --> 00:04:26.332
to the FBI, CIA,
Washington Post,

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:28.901
or how about that space case
congressman from Arizona?"

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.569
[ Laughter ]
Gosar was,

00:04:30.569 --> 00:04:33.172
along with other fringe weirdos,
like Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:34.607
one of the key instigators
of the attempt

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.943
to overturn the election results
on January 6th.

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:38.544
Greene got into a shouting match

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:40.246
on the House floor last week
with colleagues

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:42.581
during a vote to hold former
Trump advisor Steve Bannon

00:04:42.581 --> 00:04:44.483
in contempt
for defying a subpoena

00:04:44.483 --> 00:04:46.652
from the committee
investigating the insurrection.

00:04:46.652 --> 00:04:48.588
And, when she was asked
about that vote by CNN,

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:50.089
the interview took a weird turn.

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:52.558
-What was the rationale
behind your vote?

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:55.395
-The rationale behind my vote
is I'm not self-absorbed,

00:04:55.395 --> 00:04:57.830
like the rest of these jerks
here in Congress.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.565
They're all ignoring inflation.

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.400
People can hardly buy food.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.302
Gas has gone up.
-Why call them jerks,
if you don't mind --

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:04.437
-Because they're self-absorbed.

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:06.238
All they care about is Congress.

00:05:06.238 --> 00:05:07.940
They don't care
about the American people

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.441
that pay all the taxes.
-There's an attack on --

00:05:09.441 --> 00:05:12.779
-All you want to talk about is
your Trump derangement syndrome

00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:14.813
and all you want to talk
about is January 6th...
-Why are you

00:05:14.813 --> 00:05:16.315
protecting Steve Bannon?
-...where there's a riot here.

00:05:16.315 --> 00:05:17.550
-Why protect Steve Bannon?

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:20.219
-Because I care
about American people!

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:21.620
-She has the grammar and cadence

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:23.255
of the lady
at Buffalo Wild Wings,

00:05:23.255 --> 00:05:24.423
trying to get
everyone's attention

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:25.725
after one too many
Keystone Lights.

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:26.993
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:28.661
Also, you might have noticed
there was a weird ending

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:30.996
where a random dude
just wandered up next to her

00:05:30.996 --> 00:05:32.098
[ Laughter ]
during the interview.
Now,

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:33.365
if you've ever taken
the subway before,

00:05:33.365 --> 00:05:34.634
you might be thinking, "Oh, no,

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:36.268
he's about to ask her
about Scientology."

00:05:36.268 --> 00:05:37.703
[ Laughter ]
But,

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:40.339
turns out, he's another
Republican member of Congress.

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:43.809
He decided to just crash the
interview and pull Greene away.

00:05:43.809 --> 00:05:46.078
-The interview ended soon after,
when fellow

00:05:46.078 --> 00:05:48.948
Republican Congressman
Pete Sessions of Texas walked

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:52.185
into the middle
of our conversation.

00:05:52.185 --> 00:05:53.986
-So, you doing okay?
Let's get out of here.

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:55.922
-Okay. Thank you.
-But not Steve Bannon.

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:57.823
[ Laughter ]
-Wow. Even her fellow
Republicans are like,

00:05:57.823 --> 00:05:59.425
"Marjorie!

00:05:59.425 --> 00:06:00.759
Marjorie, you wandered off.

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:03.029
Maybe you should stay
away from the cameras, Marjorie.

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:05.598
[ Laughter and applause ]
Marjorie."

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:09.735
Or at the very least, Marjorie,
at the very least,

00:06:09.735 --> 00:06:11.570
use a filter
to disguise yourself."

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:13.972
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:13.972 --> 00:06:16.408
I've never seen that happen
in an interview before.

00:06:16.408 --> 00:06:17.710
You know,
doing interviews is my job.

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:19.812
It definitely doesn't help you
seem more normal.

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:22.181
If someone in a suit
came up to Andy Samberg

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:23.649
halfway through an interview
on this show and said,

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:25.417
"Hey, Andy, you okay?
Let's get out of here,"

00:06:25.417 --> 00:06:27.620
I'd definitely think,
"Something's up with Samberg,"

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.088
and then, I'd text him later
and I'd say...

00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:32.091
And he'd text back
something like...

00:06:33.225 --> 00:06:34.893
And I'd say...

00:06:34.893 --> 00:06:36.462
And then there would be like
three dots,

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:37.763
making me think he
was writing something

00:06:37.763 --> 00:06:41.067
painfully confessional,
until he just said...

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:42.535
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:44.036
I mean, seriously,
can you imagine the reaction,

00:06:44.036 --> 00:06:45.270
if, halfway
through "A Closer Look,"

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:47.739
someone just stopped me
and took me offstage?

00:06:47.739 --> 00:06:49.375
-Hey, Seth, are you okay?

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:50.609
Maybe you should go.

00:06:50.609 --> 00:06:51.744
-Why do you say that?

00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:53.512
Do I not seem okay?

00:06:53.512 --> 00:06:55.080
-Oh, no. You seem fine,
but, you see,

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:57.150
every time I say a line
on camera, I get paid,

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.651
and I need the money
to fix my pool.

00:06:58.651 --> 00:06:59.785
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:06:59.785 --> 00:07:01.220
-Your house has a pool?!

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:02.654
-[ Laughing ]
Don't be silly, Seth.

00:07:02.654 --> 00:07:04.390
My beach house has a pool.

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:05.658
[ Laughter and applause ]
The beach house

00:07:05.658 --> 00:07:07.726
Seth Meyers made.
Wink!

00:07:07.726 --> 00:07:10.763
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:12.464 --> 00:07:15.301
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:07:15.301 --> 00:07:17.136
-We're not paying you
for the [bleep] wink!

00:07:17.136 --> 00:07:18.437
[ Laughter ]

00:07:18.437 --> 00:07:19.605
You don't get money for a line

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:21.574
if it's just saying
a stage direction!

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:23.675
[ Laughter ]

00:07:23.675 --> 00:07:25.778
And, this week, Green seemed
to justify the insurrection

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:28.213
by claiming that
the Declaration of Independence

00:07:28.213 --> 00:07:29.815
says to overthrow tyrants.

00:07:29.815 --> 00:07:31.550
That apparent confession
that comes just days

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:33.285
after a bombshell report
from Rolling Stone,

00:07:33.285 --> 00:07:36.221
tying Greene to the so-called
Stop the Steal rally

00:07:36.221 --> 00:07:38.758
on January 6th,
that eventually led to the riot.

00:07:38.758 --> 00:07:41.260
Two planners of the pro-Trump
rallies, who are now cooperating

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.529
with the committee investigating
the insurrection, described...

00:07:51.704 --> 00:07:53.973
And you would
definitely remember talking

00:07:53.973 --> 00:07:55.307
[ Laughter ]
to Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:07:55.307 --> 00:07:57.342
the same way you'd remember
being attacked by Chucky.

00:07:57.342 --> 00:07:58.978
[ Laughter ]
If the cops

00:07:58.978 --> 00:08:01.213
were taking your statement
after a Chucky attack,

00:08:01.213 --> 00:08:03.482
you wouldn't say, "Oh, man,
I don't remember his name.

00:08:03.482 --> 00:08:04.583
[ Laughter ]
I think he was like --

00:08:04.583 --> 00:08:06.886
like 2'0" tall,
orange hair, overalls.

00:08:06.886 --> 00:08:09.021
[ Laughter ]
Scars all over his face.

00:08:09.021 --> 00:08:10.089
Might've been
a Cabbage Patch Kid.

00:08:10.089 --> 00:08:11.490
I don't know.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:12.925
Former mayor."

00:08:12.925 --> 00:08:15.127
[ Laughter ]
But, basically,

00:08:15.127 --> 00:08:17.196
Greene had initially responded
to the allegations

00:08:17.196 --> 00:08:18.331
by denying that she was...

00:08:27.306 --> 00:08:28.740
[ Laughter ]
They do!

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:30.542
Which is why they were writing
about you,

00:08:30.542 --> 00:08:32.944
one person who is equal to...

00:08:32.944 --> 00:08:34.313
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:34.313 --> 00:08:36.382
And, hey, I know it seems
like pandering,

00:08:36.382 --> 00:08:39.184
to reference a hot, modern band
to get an audience reaction.

00:08:39.184 --> 00:08:41.353
[ Laughter ]
But, hey,

00:08:41.353 --> 00:08:42.955
hey,

00:08:42.955 --> 00:08:44.056
we give 'em what they want.

00:08:44.056 --> 00:08:48.560
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:50.896
I'm sorry.

00:08:50.896 --> 00:08:52.164
That's a [bleep] network thing.

00:08:52.164 --> 00:08:53.399
They're cracking
on us really hard.

00:08:53.399 --> 00:08:54.733
[ Laughter ]

00:08:54.733 --> 00:08:56.335
They're like, "You haven't even
obliquely mentioned

00:08:56.335 --> 00:08:57.936
Natalie Merchant
in like two years."

00:08:57.936 --> 00:09:01.173
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:01.173 --> 00:09:02.307
If you're watching at home

00:09:02.307 --> 00:09:03.776
and you like that joke,
like reach out.

00:09:03.776 --> 00:09:06.812
[ Laughter ]

00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:10.649
"Joke."

00:09:10.649 --> 00:09:12.951
[ Laughter ]

00:09:12.951 --> 00:09:15.621
Also, her denial is itself
a damning admission.

00:09:15.621 --> 00:09:18.156
She claims she wasn't involved
in planning the protest

00:09:18.156 --> 00:09:19.458
because she was too busy trying

00:09:19.458 --> 00:09:20.893
to overturn
the election results.

00:09:20.893 --> 00:09:23.228
We shouldn't just let that
pass by unnoticed.

00:09:23.228 --> 00:09:24.563
It's a classic defense --

00:09:24.563 --> 00:09:26.198
[ As Greene ] I couldn't have
burned down your house

00:09:26.198 --> 00:09:28.567
because I was too busy
buying gasoline and matches

00:09:28.567 --> 00:09:30.001
and a map to your house.

00:09:30.001 --> 00:09:31.203
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:31.203 --> 00:09:33.705
But probably the worst
non-denial denial came

00:09:33.705 --> 00:09:35.608
from Alabama
Congressman Mo Brooks,

00:09:35.608 --> 00:09:37.209
one of the most vocal advocates
of the big lie,

00:09:37.209 --> 00:09:38.577
and another coconspirator

00:09:38.577 --> 00:09:40.379
who was also implicated
in the Rolling Stone article.

00:09:40.379 --> 00:09:42.148
Brooks said,
in response, that...

00:09:48.821 --> 00:09:50.590
[ Laughter ]

00:09:55.294 --> 00:09:57.229
Wow, he O.J.'d his own staff.

00:09:57.229 --> 00:09:59.097
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:59.097 --> 00:10:01.834
"I didn't do it, but,
if my staff did, here's how."

00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:03.769
[ Laughter ]

00:10:03.769 --> 00:10:05.904
It's a really nice joke
that we just told,

00:10:05.904 --> 00:10:07.740
like that we changed
what O.J.'ing means,

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:09.275
to mean like writing a book.

00:10:09.275 --> 00:10:11.644
[ Laughter ]

00:10:11.644 --> 00:10:12.845
Like for a long time,
it's been like,

00:10:12.845 --> 00:10:13.946
"I feel like,
when people say O.J.'ing,

00:10:13.946 --> 00:10:15.014
you know, they think..."

00:10:15.014 --> 00:10:16.382
[ Laughter ]

00:10:16.382 --> 00:10:17.750
You know, to O.J. someone is

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.652
to write a piece
of speculative fiction.

00:10:19.652 --> 00:10:22.288
[ Laughter ]

00:10:22.288 --> 00:10:25.523
For me, it's like author,
football, and then, [ Mutters ]

00:10:25.523 --> 00:10:28.694
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:31.697 --> 00:10:33.532
Brooks really threw his staff
under the bus,

00:10:33.532 --> 00:10:35.134
although, in fairness,
I do that a lot

00:10:35.134 --> 00:10:37.102
with my staff,
when a joke bombs.

00:10:37.102 --> 00:10:39.838
Like I had no involvement
with that 10,000 Maniacs joke.

00:10:39.838 --> 00:10:41.340
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:42.941
But I'm proud
of whoever wrote it.

00:10:42.941 --> 00:10:44.376
Took a lot of guts!

00:10:44.376 --> 00:10:46.912
[ Laughter ]

00:10:46.912 --> 00:10:48.981
Took a lot of guts to go there
in a room full of people.

00:10:48.981 --> 00:10:51.383
[ Laughter ]

00:10:51.383 --> 00:10:52.818
Now, if you're not familiar
with Mo Brooks,

00:10:52.818 --> 00:10:54.520
he's the extremely
pro-Trump congressman

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:56.889
who gave an incendiary speech
calling on Trump supporters

00:10:56.889 --> 00:10:58.958
to "start taking down names
and kicking ass,"

00:10:58.958 --> 00:11:01.160
then, said he only did it
because Trump told him to.

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:04.162
He metaphorically ran
away from a lawsuit

00:11:04.162 --> 00:11:05.764
over his involvement
in the insurrection

00:11:05.764 --> 00:11:08.333
and literally ran
away from a reporter

00:11:08.333 --> 00:11:09.768
who tried to ask him
about his support

00:11:09.768 --> 00:11:12.771
for accused sexual predator
Roy Moore in 2017.

00:11:12.771 --> 00:11:14.840
[ Running footsteps clacking ]

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:19.812
[ Laughter ]

00:11:26.385 --> 00:11:28.687
Yeah, that definitely seems
like the kind of guy

00:11:28.687 --> 00:11:30.155
who would incite
an insurrection,

00:11:30.155 --> 00:11:31.657
blame his staff,
and then, I guess,

00:11:31.657 --> 00:11:33.125
judging
from the clacking sound,

00:11:33.125 --> 00:11:34.659
escape on horseback.

00:11:34.659 --> 00:11:35.961
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:35.961 --> 00:11:39.031
Seriously, the Foley work
on that clip is outstanding.

00:11:39.031 --> 00:11:40.899
Why does it sound like
they're galloping into town

00:11:40.899 --> 00:11:42.134
on a Mustang?

00:11:42.134 --> 00:11:43.702
[ Hooves clopping ]
I didn't invade or riot,

00:11:43.702 --> 00:11:44.970
but, if my staff did,

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:46.405
I'd be proud of him.

00:11:46.405 --> 00:11:48.340
[ Laughter ]
Now, if you'll excuse me,

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:50.643
me and Old Thunder, here,

00:11:50.643 --> 00:11:52.177
we'll be down in the saloon,

00:11:52.177 --> 00:11:54.380
drinking a sarsaparilla
and getting our next mission

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:56.681
from weird old Abe Lincoln.

00:11:56.681 --> 00:11:57.950
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:01.153
The core --

00:12:01.153 --> 00:12:02.654
The core of today's
Republican Party

00:12:02.654 --> 00:12:04.423
is the big lie
that the election was stolen.

00:12:04.423 --> 00:12:05.958
They tried to overthrow
the results.

00:12:05.958 --> 00:12:07.926
They're being open about it,
trying to justify it,

00:12:07.926 --> 00:12:09.028
and planning on doing it again,

00:12:09.028 --> 00:12:10.262
which is why they have
to be stopped.

00:12:10.262 --> 00:12:12.498
One of our two major parties,
a party poised

00:12:12.498 --> 00:12:14.366
to take back power,
if Democrats fail,

00:12:14.366 --> 00:12:16.101
has been captured
by a cult-like movement

00:12:16.101 --> 00:12:24.809
of weirdos, authoritarians,
and scoundrels.

00:12:24.809 --> 00:12:25.911
You don't get used to it.

00:12:25.911 --> 00:12:27.012
[ Laughter ]

00:12:27.012 --> 00:12:28.313
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:28.313 --> 00:12:32.184
♪♪

